%S A398691 1,2,3,4,5,4,6,7,8,9,10,10,11,12,11,13,14,14,15,15,16,17,18,18,19,20,
%T A398691 21,21,22,22,23,24,25,26,26,27,28,29,30,31,32,30,33,34,33,35,36,36,37,
%U A398691 38,39,40,41,41,42,42,43,44,45,45,46,47,48,49,50,48
%N A398691 a(n) is the maximum size of a subset S of {1,...,n} that contains n and in which no two distinct x, y in S have x+y dividing 2*x*y.
%C A398691 The condition "(x+y) | 2*x*y" says that the harmonic mean of x and y is an integer.
%C A398691 This is the "n in S" refinement of A398582, suggested by _Andrew Howroyd_: A398582(n) = Max_{k=1..n} a(k), so A398582 is the running maximum of this sequence. This sequence is not monotonic (a(5) = 5 > a(6) = 4) and it lies strictly below its running maximum for 148 of the first 1200 indices.
%H A398691 William Alexander Carney, <a href="/A398691/b398691.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1200</a>
%H A398691 Thomas Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/327">Problem 327</a>, Erdős Problems.
%H A398691 William Alexander Carney, <a href="/A398691/a398691.py.txt">Python program (exact solver: forced-n independent set via minimum vertex cover and zero-gap MILP, every witness re-checked against the definition)</a>
%e A398691 a(6) = 4: S = {1, 4, 5, 6} contains 6, and for every pair of distinct elements x, y the sum x+y does not divide 2*x*y (the six sums are 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11 and the corresponding products 2*x*y are 8, 10, 12, 40, 48, 60). No 5-element subset of {1,...,6} containing 6 has this property, so a(6) = 4 < a(5) = 5.
%Y A398691 Cf. A398582 (same condition without requiring n in S; equals the running maximum of this sequence), A384927.
%K A398691 nonn,new
%O A398691 1,2
%A A398691 _William Alexander Carney_, Aug 16 2026
